To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the Georgia Open Records Act, I hereby request the following records:

GEORGIA OPEN RECORDS ACT REQUEST

Subject: Documentary Chain of Creditor, Assignment, Transfer, Servicing, Collection, Representation, and Court Administration — Fulton County State Court Civil Action Nos. 09VS163162 and 10VS180130

To the Custodian of Records / State Court of Fulton County — Civil Division:
Pursuant to the Georgia Open Records Act, O.C.G.A. § 50-18-70 et seq., I request access to existing public records concerning the administrative, filing, docketing, case-management, creditor-identification, assignment, transfer, servicing, collection, representation, and related handling of the following Fulton County State Court proceedings:
	•	Civil Action No. 09VS163162
	•	Civil Action No. 10VS180130

The request is directed principally toward existing records that may permit reconstruction of the documented chain of entities associated with the claim or alleged debt underlying these proceedings, including, where reflected in existing records, the original plaintiff or creditor, any assignee, purchaser, transferee, servicer, collector, agent, fiduciary, trustee, attorney, law firm, or other entity appearing in the Court's records as acting for or on behalf of any such entity.

This request does not assume that any particular assignment, sale, transfer, servicing arrangement, fiduciary relationship, account-control change, debt purchase, consolidation, or other transaction occurred. Instead, it seeks existing records that document whether any such event was reflected in the Court's records.

The requester is not asking the Clerk or Court to determine the legal ownership of any debt, the validity or legal effect of any assignment or transfer, the existence of an agency or fiduciary relationship, the legal authority of any entity, or whether any particular transaction was legally effective. The request seeks the existing records from which such factual matters, if documented, may be determined.


I. IDENTIFIED PROCEEDINGS
Please process this request separately for:
	1	Civil Action No. 09VS163162
	2	Civil Action No. 10VS180130

Civil Action No. 10VS180130
The requester possesses a copy of the Court's September 19, 2023 Order Regarding Defendant's Request for Copies of Pleadings.
That order identifies Bank of America, N.A. as Plaintiff and Charles DeLozier as Defendant.

The order states that:
	•	the underlying action was filed on July 12, 2010;
	•	the action sought $39,544.03 in principal and $40,928.70 in prejudgment interest;
	•	the Marshal's Entry of Service filed July 26, 2010 indicated that Defendant was not served; and
	•	the matter was dismissed by Plaintiff on September 13, 2011.

The order identifies Douglas L. Brooks, Bar No. 084725, as counsel for Bank of America, N.A.
The requester also possesses an electronic filing/service record concerning the September 19, 2023 order, described further below in Section XIV.

Civil Action No. 09VS163162
The requester has identified Court records reflecting:
Southeastern Resolution Corp. AGN Chase Bank USA NA
as Plaintiff.

The requester has also identified David A. Kleber and Bedard Law Group PC in connection with that representation.
The requester does not rely upon those identifiers as establishing the legal ownership, assignment, servicing, collection, or agency relationship of any entity. They are provided as search aids for locating existing Court records.


II. PURPOSE AND SCOPE OF REQUEST
The purpose of this request is to obtain existing records sufficient to reconstruct, from the Court's records, the documented history of:
original creditor or claimant → plaintiff → assignment or transfer, if any → purchaser or transferee, if any → servicer, if any → collection entity, if any → agent, fiduciary, trustee, or other representative, if any → attorney or law firm → entity that initiated or prosecuted the action → subsequent changes in representation or authority → dismissal or other disposition.

The requester is not asking the Clerk to create this chain.
The requester seeks the underlying existing records from which such a chain, if documented, may be established.
This request includes both substantive records filed in or maintained with the case files and administrative or electronic records concerning the creation, maintenance, processing, filing, service, representation, and disposition of the cases.


III. ORIGINAL PLAINTIFF, CREDITOR, CLAIMANT, AND ACCOUNT IDENTITY
For each case, please provide existing records identifying, where such information is maintained or reflected:
	•	the original plaintiff;
	•	the creditor;
	•	the claimant;
	•	the account owner;
	•	the entity alleged to own the debt or claim;
	•	the entity alleged to have authority to collect;
	•	the entity alleged to have authority to prosecute or enforce the claim;
	•	any predecessor entity;
	•	any successor entity; and
	•	any other entity identified as having an interest in or authority concerning the claim.

Responsive records may include, where maintained:
	•	party-information records;
	•	docket information;
	•	pleadings;
	•	affidavits;
	•	exhibits;
	•	notices;
	•	certificates;
	•	administrative records;
	•	electronic case-management records;
	•	party-history records; and
	•	other existing records containing such information.


IV. DOCUMENTED CREDITOR, CLAIMANT, AND ENTITY HISTORY
Please provide existing records maintained by or filed with the Court that identify, reference, or document any change involving the creditor, claimant, plaintiff, account owner, assignee, purchaser, transferee, servicer, collector, agent, fiduciary, trustee, or other entity associated with the claim.

This includes records concerning any documented:
	•	assignment;
	•	transfer;
	•	sale;
	•	purchase;
	•	acquisition;
	•	conveyance;
	•	portfolio transfer;
	•	receivable transfer;
	•	debt sale;
	•	servicing transfer;
	•	collection transfer;
	•	substitution of plaintiff;
	•	substitution of creditor;
	•	change of claimant;
	•	change of account owner; or
	•	other change in the identity or authority of an entity associated with the claim.


V. ASSIGNMENTS, TRANSFERS, SALES, AND PURCHASES
Please provide existing records concerning any assignment, transfer, sale, purchase, acquisition, or other conveyance of the alleged debt or claim.

This includes, where filed or maintained:
	•	assignments;
	•	assignments of accounts;
	•	bills of sale;
	•	purchase agreements;
	•	transfer schedules;
	•	exhibits identifying transferred accounts;
	•	assignment affidavits;
	•	ownership affidavits;
	•	declarations;
	•	certifications;
	•	notices of assignment;
	•	notices of transfer;
	•	motions concerning assignment or transfer;
	•	substitutions;
	•	amendments; and
	•	orders concerning any such transaction.

If an assignment or transfer is referenced in a responsive Court record but the underlying transaction document is not maintained by the Clerk, please provide the existing record that references or identifies the transaction.


VI. DEBT PURCHASERS AND SUCCESSOR ENTITIES
Please provide existing records identifying any entity that appears in the Court records as having purchased, acquired, received, or otherwise obtained an interest in the alleged debt or claim.

This includes entities described in existing records as, or performing functions associated with:
	•	debt purchaser;
	•	purchaser of receivables;
	•	assignee;
	•	transferee;
	•	successor creditor;
	•	successor claimant;
	•	portfolio purchaser;
	•	collection purchaser;
	•	account purchaser; or
	•	similar designation.
The request does not assume that any such entity existed.


VII. SERVICER, COLLECTION ENTITIES, AND OTHER INTERMEDIARIES
Please provide existing records identifying any entity that appears in connection with either case as:
	•	servicer;
	•	sub-servicer;
	•	collection agency;
	•	debt collector;
	•	collection representative;
	•	account administrator;
	•	payment processor;
	•	account manager;
	•	agent;
	•	authorized representative;
	•	fiduciary;
	•	trustee;
	•	custodian; or
	•	other intermediary acting for or on behalf of a creditor, claimant, plaintiff, assignee, purchaser, or transferee.

For each such entity, please provide the existing record establishing or describing the entity's documented role.


VIII. AUTHORITY TO ACT AND REPRESENTATION
Please provide existing records concerning authority to act for the plaintiff, creditor, claimant, assignee, purchaser, servicer, collection entity, or other entity associated with either case.
This includes, where maintained:
	•	powers of attorney;
	•	agency appointments;
	•	servicing authorizations;
	•	collection authorizations;
	•	fiduciary appointments;
	•	trustee appointments;
	•	representative appointments;
	•	authorizations to file suit;
	•	authorizations to prosecute;
	•	authorizations to dismiss;
	•	authorizations to settle;
	•	authorizations to collect; and
	•	comparable records.

The request seeks the existing record documenting or referring to such authority. It does not ask the Clerk to determine whether the authority was legally sufficient or effective.


IX. ATTORNEYS, LAW FIRMS, AND REPRESENTATION HISTORY
Please provide existing records identifying every attorney or law firm appearing in either case for the plaintiff, creditor, assignee, purchaser, servicer, collector, or other claimant.

For each attorney or firm, please provide existing information showing, where maintained:
	•	attorney name;
	•	bar number;
	•	law firm;
	•	entity represented;
	•	date of appearance;
	•	date of withdrawal;
	•	substitution;
	•	change of representation;
	•	filing activity;
	•	service information;
	•	and any documented change in the entity represented.

The requester has identified the following attorneys and firms as search aids:
	•	Douglas L. Brooks, Bar No. 084725, identified in connection with Bank of America, N.A. in Civil Action No. 10VS180130.
	•	David A. Kleber, identified in connection with Bedard Law Group PC and Southeastern Resolution Corp. AGN Chase Bank USA NA in Civil Action No. 09VS163162.

Please search existing Court and e-filing records using these names and, where maintained, associated bar numbers, law-firm information, professional contact information, service-contact information, filing-user information, and other existing identifiers.

The requester does not seek private or personal contact information merely because such information may exist in a responsive record. The purpose of providing these names is to assist the Clerk in locating responsive records.

The inclusion of these names does not imply that either attorney or firm performed any act beyond what is reflected in existing records.


X. CASE 10VS180130 — BANK OF AMERICA, N.A.
For Civil Action No. 10VS180130, please provide existing records concerning:
	•	Bank of America, N.A.;
	•	any predecessor or successor entity;
	•	any assignee;
	•	any purchaser;
	•	any servicer;
	•	any collection entity;
	•	any attorney;
	•	any law firm;
	•	any agent;
	•	and any other entity documented as acting for or on behalf of Bank of America, N.A.

Please include existing records concerning the filing of the action, prosecution of the action, service processing, representation, dismissal, and any documented change in the identity or authority of an entity associated with the claim.


XI. CASE 09VS163162 — SOUTHEASTERN RESOLUTION CORP. / CHASE BANK USA NA
For Civil Action No. 09VS163162, please provide existing records concerning:
Southeastern Resolution Corp. AGN Chase Bank USA NA
and any documented relationship among:
	•	Southeastern Resolution Corp.;
	•	Chase Bank USA NA;
	•	any predecessor or successor entity;
	•	any assignee;
	•	any purchaser;
	•	any servicer;
	•	any collection entity;
	•	any attorney;
	•	any law firm; and
	•	any other entity identified as acting for or on behalf of the plaintiff or creditor.

Please provide the existing records that identify or describe the nature of any such relationship.
The requester does not ask the Clerk to determine the legal relationship between these entities.


XII. POSSIBLE RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN 09VS163162 AND 10VS180130
Please search existing records for any documented connection between Civil Action No. 09VS163162 and Civil Action No. 10VS180130.

This includes records showing whether the cases were:
	•	consolidated;
	•	administratively linked;
	•	cross-referenced;
	•	transferred;
	•	reassigned;
	•	associated;
	•	treated as related cases;
	•	entered into a common workflow;
	•	referenced in administrative notes; or
	•	otherwise connected.

Please also search for records in either case that identify or reference the other case number.
The requester does not assert that the cases were consolidated or otherwise legally related.


XIII. ACCOUNT CONTROL, SERVICING, AND COLLECTION AUTHORITY
Please provide existing records concerning any documented change in:
	•	account control;
	•	collection authority;
	•	servicing authority;
	•	plaintiff authority;
	•	creditor authority;
	•	attorney authority;
	•	agency authority;
	•	fiduciary authority;
	•	trustee authority; or
	•	other authority concerning the alleged debt or claim.

The term "account control" is used solely to identify existing records concerning documented changes in control, servicing, collection, or authority.
The requester is not asking the Clerk to determine whether any alleged transfer or change was legally effective.


XIV. FILINGS AND EXHIBITS CONCERNING OWNERSHIP OR AUTHORITY
Please provide existing pleadings, motions, affidavits, exhibits, notices, certificates, correspondence, or other filed records concerning:
	•	ownership;
	•	assignment;
	•	transfer;
	•	purchase;
	•	servicing;
	•	collection;
	•	agency;
	•	fiduciary status;
	•	trustee status;
	•	authority to collect;
	•	authority to sue;
	•	authority to prosecute;
	•	authority to dismiss;
	•	substitution;
	•	or changes in plaintiff or creditor.


XV. E-FILING AND ADMINISTRATIVE TRANSACTION RECORDS
The requester possesses the following e-filing information concerning the September 19, 2023 order in Civil Action No. 10VS180130:
	•	Case Number: 10VS180130
	•	Case Style: BANK OF AMERICA VS DELOZIER, CHARLES
	•	Date/Time Submitted: September 19, 2023, 12:31 PM EST
	•	Filing Type: Order
	•	Filing Description: Order Regarding Defendant's Request for Copies of Pleadings
	•	Filed By: Joshua Saunders
	•	Service Contact: Charles DeLozier
	•	Other Service Contact Not Associated With a Party on the Case: Joshua Saunders

Please provide existing e-filing, case-management, service, or administrative records sufficient to establish, where maintained:
	•	the filing transaction;
	•	filing submission;
	•	filing acceptance;
	•	docketing;
	•	filing user/account;
	•	document metadata;
	•	service transaction;
	•	service recipients;
	•	recipient categories;
	•	recipient additions or removals;
	•	service status;
	•	transaction identifiers;
	•	and any administrative history associated with this filing.

The requester provides the foregoing transaction information as a specific search identifier and does not seek disclosure of private contact information merely because such information may appear in the underlying transaction record.


XVI. NON-PARTY SERVICE CONTACTS
Please provide existing records sufficient to establish how individuals or accounts not associated with a named party were added to or associated with service or notification transactions in either case.

This request includes existing records concerning:
	•	court employees;
	•	judicial assistants;
	•	judges' offices;
	•	Clerk's Office personnel;
	•	case-management personnel;
	•	courtroom administrators;
	•	attorneys;
	•	law-firm personnel;
	•	collection personnel;
	•	creditor personnel; and
	•	other non-party service contacts.

For each such record, please provide, where maintained:
	•	name;
	•	professional or official email address, where maintained as part of the relevant record;
	•	official role or affiliation;
	•	date added;
	•	date removed;
	•	associated filing;
	•	associated transaction;
	•	user/account responsible for the change;
	•	source of the contact information;
	•	and administrative notes concerning the change.
The requester does not seek private personnel information.


XVII. SERVICE AND NOTIFICATION HISTORY
Please provide existing records showing service or notification transactions concerning filings in either case, including, where maintained:
	•	date and time;
	•	document served;
	•	recipients;
	•	recipient category;
	•	service method;
	•	delivery status;
	•	transaction identifier;
	•	initiating user/account;
	•	additions or removals; and
	•	error or exception information.
Please include historical recipient information where such history is maintained.


XVIII. ADMINISTRATIVE AND CASE-RELATED COMMUNICATIONS
Please provide existing emails, electronic messages, correspondence, administrative notes, help-desk requests, filing-support communications, or other existing communications concerning the administrative or ministerial handling of either case, including communications concerning:
	•	creditor identity;
	•	plaintiff identity;
	•	assignment;
	•	transfer;
	•	purchase;
	•	servicing;
	•	collection;
	•	attorney representation;
	•	substitution;
	•	dismissal;
	•	case linkage;
	•	service;
	•	notification;
	•	filing;
	•	docketing;
	•	party information;
	•	attorney information;
	•	or changes to case or party information.

Please search using, where reasonably necessary:
	•	09VS163162;
	•	10VS180130;
	•	Bank of America, N.A.;
	•	Chase Bank USA NA;
	•	Southeastern Resolution Corp.;
	•	Charles DeLozier;
	•	Douglas L. Brooks;
	•	David A. Kleber;
	•	Bedard Law Group PC;
	•	Joshua Saunders; and
	•	other names or entities appearing in responsive Court records.

The requester recognizes that a responsive communication may concern a case without containing the case number in its subject line or body. The request is nevertheless limited to communications concerning the identified proceedings and the administrative, filing, service, representation, creditor-identification, or related matters described in this request.
The request does not seek judicial deliberations, judicial mental impressions, draft decisions, legal analysis, or protected judicial work product.


XIX. DISMISSAL AND FINAL CASE ADMINISTRATION
For Civil Action No. 10VS180130, please provide existing records concerning the September 13, 2011 dismissal, including, where maintained:
	•	dismissal filing;
	•	filing transaction;
	•	filing user;
	•	filing date/time;
	•	docketing;
	•	administrative processing;
	•	plaintiff information;
	•	attorney information;
	•	user/action history;
	•	and existing communications or administrative notes concerning the dismissal.
Please provide comparable disposition and final-administration records for Civil Action No. 09VS163162.


XX. ELECTRONIC CASE-MANAGEMENT AND AUDIT HISTORY
Where maintained, please provide existing electronic records sufficient to establish:
	•	case creation;
	•	party creation;
	•	party modification;
	•	plaintiff modification;
	•	creditor or claimant modification;
	•	attorney entry;
	•	attorney removal;
	•	attorney substitution;
	•	case assignment;
	•	case reassignment;
	•	filing transactions;
	•	document uploads;
	•	document replacements;
	•	docketing;
	•	status changes;
	•	administrative notes;
	•	service transactions;
	•	recipient changes;
	•	and other documented administrative events.
This includes existing audit trails, transaction histories, workflow histories, user/action histories, or comparable information that is reasonably retrievable through existing system functions.


XXI. SEARCH FOR THIRD-PARTY, SUCCESSOR, OR INTERMEDIARY ENTITIES
Please search the existing Court records for any entity appearing in connection with either case that was not the originally identified plaintiff but was subsequently identified as:
	•	creditor;
	•	assignee;
	•	purchaser;
	•	transferee;
	•	successor;
	•	servicer;
	•	collector;
	•	debt buyer;
	•	fiduciary;
	•	trustee;
	•	agent;
	•	representative;
	•	administrator; or
	•	other entity acting concerning the claim.
Please provide the existing record in which each such entity appears and the role or relationship reflected in that record.
This request does not assume that any such entity existed.


XXII. EXISTING-RECORD LIMITATION
This request seeks existing records only.
It does not ask the Clerk to:
	•	create a new creditor-history report;
	•	construct a new chronology;
	•	determine the legal owner of a debt;
	•	determine whether an assignment was legally valid;
	•	determine whether an entity had standing;
	•	determine whether a debt purchaser lawfully acquired an account;
	•	determine whether an entity was legally a debt collector;
	•	determine whether an attorney was properly authorized;
	•	reconstruct undocumented events;
	•	answer interrogatories;
	•	provide legal advice; or
	•	reach a legal conclusion.
Where information exists in a filing, exhibit, affidavit, docket entry, administrative note, database field, audit record, service record, email, or other existing record, that existing record is requested.
If a particular requested record does not exist, please identify that the requested record does not exist rather than treating the request as asking the Clerk to create a new record.


XXIII. ELECTRONIC RECORDS AND THIRD-PARTY SYSTEMS
Where responsive information is maintained electronically, please provide it electronically in the format in which it is ordinarily maintained or in a standard export format supported by the existing system.
This request includes existing:
	•	data fields;
	•	timestamps;
	•	transaction identifiers;
	•	audit records;
	•	workflow records;
	•	filing metadata;
	•	user/action information;
	•	party information;
	•	attorney information;
	•	service information;
	•	recipient information; and
	•	document-history information.
If responsive records are maintained electronically by a private vendor or other entity performing a service or function for or on behalf of the Court, please process the request to the extent provided by applicable law.


XXIV. SEGREGABILITY AND EXEMPTIONS
If a responsive record contains exempt information, please redact only the portion for which a specific exemption applies and provide the remaining reasonably segregable information.
For any withheld record or portion, please identify the specific statutory authority supporting the withholding, including the applicable Code section and subsection or paragraph where applicable.
The requester does not seek disclosure of information that Georgia law expressly protects.


XXV. PRODUCTION AND RESPONSE
Please provide responsive records electronically through the MuckRock request portal or by another electronic method reasonably available to the Clerk's Office.
If responsive records cannot be produced within the applicable statutory period, please provide the required description of the responsive records and anticipated production timeline.
If fees are expected to exceed the applicable statutory threshold, please provide the required cost estimate before incurring such charges.
If a particular category is considered unusually broad or difficult to locate, please identify the specific category at issue and, where appropriate, indicate what narrower identification would permit the responsive records to be located.
The requester is willing to receive responsive records in installments or by category.


XXVI. PRESERVATION OF RESPONSIVE RECORDS
Because this request specifically concerns historical electronic case-management information, filing transactions, service histories, recipient histories, administrative notes, communications, and audit information, please preserve existing responsive records pending completion of this request to the extent permitted and required by applicable law and applicable records-retention obligations.
This request does not ask the Clerk to create a preservation report or other new record.


XXVII. NO ASSUMPTION OF UNDERLYING EVENTS
For avoidance of doubt, this request does not assert that:
	•	Bank of America, N.A. sold or assigned the claim;
	•	Chase Bank USA NA sold or assigned the claim;
	•	Southeastern Resolution Corp. purchased or serviced the claim;
	•	a debt buyer acquired the claim;
	•	a third party assumed account control;
	•	a fiduciary relationship existed;
	•	a servicing relationship existed;
	•	the two cases were consolidated;
	•	the cases were otherwise legally related; or
	•	any particular attorney or entity acted outside the role reflected in the existing Court records.

The purpose of this request is to obtain the existing documentary and electronic record from which those factual questions, to the extent documented in Court records, may be determined.

This request is limited to existing records and does not ask the Clerk to create a new factual history, legal determination, or conclusion.

Respectfully,

/s/ Charles Stanley DeLozier Jr.

Charles Stanley DeLozier Jr., pro se

The requested documents will be made available to the general public, and this request is not being made for commercial purposes.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request. I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not.

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 3 business days, as the statute requires.

Sincerely,

Charles Stanley DeLozier Jr.

